# Cloudflare Pages redirects (decision #7; replaces netlify.toml). Unknown paths outside the planner already fall back
# to the home page, because the site has no 404.html. The first rule that matches wins, and a 200 rule serves the file
# at its target without looking at these rules again.
# The switch (#18, design §3 and §11, 14 Oct): /planner/ and everything under it open the new planner, whose files live
# under /app/ (built into web/app/). Its page is /app/, not /app/index.html: Cloudflare drops a rule that proxies to a
# path ending in /index.html as an infinite loop.
# The addresses used while it was built, /planner/next/..., move to the same address under /planner/ (301), so old
# links and bookmarks still work.
# The old planner, the way back, opens at /planner/old/: its file, web/planner/index.html, is served there as it is.
# Going back is one change: make the last line `/planner/*   /planner/   200` again (the old planner at /planner/).
/planner/next     /planner/           301
/planner/next/*   /planner/:splat     301
/planner/old      /planner/old/       301
/planner/old/*    /planner/           200
/planner          /planner/           301
/planner/*        /app/               200
